      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "There is currently no way to indicate to the ScrollController, that it's content is stale, and that it should re-calculate it's extents.\r\n\r\nThis is necessary as I'm building a scrollbar, that relies on maxExtents to control a list. When the contents of the list change, maxExtents does not update, until a scrollEvent has been triggered. \r\n\r\nYou can hack around this, by using antimateTo, and  moving it like 1px, but if the list is too short, this does not work since the list can not be scrolled. \r\n\r\n**Can you provide an API on ScrollController for triggering this calculation?** ",
